      "writtenOn": "2019-03-23T07:24:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ooh this needs comments. This logic relies on the fact that the update of NetworkCapabilities cannot have changed the return value of shouldApplyInterfaceFiltering between before and after, because it\u0027s only using getEstablishingVpnAppUid() which happens to never change in an NetworkCapabilities update across the life of a single network.\n\nIf it COULD change, then you\u0027d have the possible case where the filtering was previously needed and not any more, and then you would omit removing the ranges.\n\nSo here you have code using shouldApplyInterfaceFiltering that actively depends on the implementation details of that method, so I think you even need comments inside shouldApplyInterfaceFiltering to indicate that, otherwise someone looking to change its implementation will not notice they are breaking this code. Maybe it\u0027s actually safer to even write the code here as if this could change.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5823,
        "startChar": 41,
        "endLine": 5823,
        "endChar": 70
      },
      "revId": "f618071959fc410d7e7b02fa2e6574bac1c4e9a1",
