    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c2d54968_c69af9be",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/PermissionMonitor.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 95,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-23T07:24:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "High-level question : it seems when we program the UIDs for filtering into netd, we pass the interface, but when we remove them we don\u0027t have to. I think that\u0027s because an interface corresponds to one VPN which can only be running for a single user at a time, therefore the UID actually specifies the interface. But of course netd still has to know the interface when adding.\n\nBut here we can know the interface names whenever we want, so do we actually need to keep this map, or would a simple set of ranges do ?\nEven assuming it\u0027s possible, I\u0027m not clear on whether that would actually simplify the code – just wanted to submit this for consideration.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 95,
        "startChar": 45,
        "endLine": 95,
        "endChar": 58
      },
      "revId": "f618071959fc410d7e7b02fa2e6574bac1c4e9a1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ac2c3258_960aeca4",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/PermissionMonitor.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 95,
      "author": {
        "id": 1059499
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-27T01:00:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My gut feeling is that it\u0027s better to have the information to flow from CS -\u003e PermissionMonitor -\u003e netd. That way we can keep data consistent, albeit with a bit of duplication. If we lose the uid-\u003eifname information here, Permission Monitor has to call back to CS when that\u0027s needed, and it might cause subtle races: by the time PermissionMontior calls to CS, the network might have already changed.",
      "parentUuid": "c2d54968_c69af9be",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 95,
        "startChar": 45,
        "endLine": 95,
        "endChar": 58
      },
